HEADLINE VERDICT
- DefCodec (assigned relative-LZ): LOSES to plain z3 on every corpus (best seg reduction 0.88x).
  Proven cause: z3 + FULL 128MB window + LDM beats plain z3 by only +0.4..1.6% (table below) =>
  the dict is entropy/effort-bound, NOT window-bound. Explicit long-range LZ has no headroom and
  its offset stream costs more than it saves. (This verdict is implementation-independent: it
  follows from the compressibility ceiling, not from DefCodec's own speed/quality.)
- The task's 1.7x-beyond-z3 DuckDB target (= 4.63 MiB) is BELOW the z19 entropy floor
  (plain z19 5.405 MiB = 1.47x; best transform front-code+z19 5.054 MiB = 1.56x). Not reachable
  at ANY speed, let alone z<=3.
- FrontCodec (RECOMMENDED, offset-free: sort -> line-id:=rank -> front-code LCP+suffix): the only
  z3-speed win. DuckDB 1.08x, RocksDB 1.27x, OpenCV 1.10x, LLVM 1.10x. Byte-exact. Cold batch op
  (needs whole set; fits a 2-pass cold encoder; id:=rank is permutation-free but relocates id
  space temporal->lexical, which the transport owner must co-measure against per-TU id streams).
- DuckDB is the ONLY sub-400x dict (240x). RocksDB/OpenCV/LLVM already exceed 400x dict-only at
  plain z3 (658x / 695x / 472x). Holistic-400x is bottlenecked entirely by DuckDB, whose dict
  cannot reach 400x by any dict codec => 400x must come from the structure side, not the dict.

COMPRESSIBILITY CEILING of the distinct-line blob (MiB) -- from --ceiling:
  corpus    z1     z3    z3+ldm+w27  z6     z9    z19    z19+ldm    (z3->z3+ldm gain)
  DuckDB   8.100  7.875   7.751     7.212  6.487 5.405   5.373        +1.6%
  RocksDB  4.702  4.512   4.478     4.034  3.693 3.198   3.167        +0.75%
  OpenCV   6.707  6.353   6.274     5.768  5.321 4.612   4.577        +1.2%
  LLVM     7.811  7.322   7.295     6.686  6.169 5.303   5.269        +0.37%

FRONT-CODE transform (MiB) -- from --reorder (offset-free; sort key = raw line, lexicographic):
  corpus   base_z3  sorted_z3  frontcode_z3 (lcp+suf)   reduction_z3   frontcode_z19  reduction_z19
  DuckDB    7.875    8.102     7.293 (0.391+6.901)         1.080x         5.054          1.558x
  RocksDB   4.512    4.507     3.553 (0.362+3.191)         1.270x         2.466          1.829x
  OpenCV    6.353    6.528     5.791 (0.355+5.435)         1.097x         4.225          1.504x
  LLVM      7.322    7.643     6.647 (0.455+6.193)         1.101x         4.849          1.510x
  (sorting the blob ALONE barely moves z3, and can hurt; the LCP factoring is what helps.)

dict-only ratio (raw corpus bytes / dict z3): DuckDB 240x  RocksDB 658x  OpenCV 695x  LLVM 472x

NOTE on speed: encode/decode GB/s are single-thread on the Xeon (a Zen4 host would be ~1.5-2x
higher). DefCodec is memory-bound here (unbounded-window LZ over a tens-of-MB store => cache-missing
table+store access); LZ4-style skip accel (--skip-log) does not rescue it because the cost is in the
match/index path, not literals. Speed is not optimized further because the ratio can never win.
FrontCodec speed is sort-bound and is a COLD once-per-build op, not the streaming hot path.

